#
# ARM: warm-all-lru-reactive, held fixed. Chosen on measurement, not taste. It is the only warming
# arm that NEVER crossed in any committed cell: its CAL1F cell at 4,511.7 uncached tok/s is the
# highest non-crossing cell in the entire 56-cell set, and its EP-G cell sits at 0.446 s, while it
# still produces 91.3 percent warm requests on EP-G. So it generates the warm rows the held-out
# split needs without itself leaving the healthy regime, which is what a healthy-regime warm fit
# requires. The committed by_arm split failed precisely by holding out arms with zero warm rows.
#
# LOAD LEVER: device count n, which is exogenous to the policy. A policy-driven lever would confound
# load with the quantity being priced.
#
# WORKLOAD: EP-G + per-frame at the 3 s deadline (_L3_epg in the tag), so the fit regime matches the
# regime MARGIN_CF is scored in.
#
# THE EDGE IS ENFORCED AFTER THE FACT, NOT GUESSED. Requests are classified by their own 100 s
# window's first-token p50: healthy at or below 2.781 s, unclassified to 31.0 s, collapsed above.
# Only healthy windows are fitted or tested. n=20 is the one that may cross (a committed n20 cell of
# another arm reached 5,444 tok/s and a 77 s window), so this sweep BRACKETS the edge rather than
# being designed to reach collapse. If n=20 crosses, its healthy windows still contribute and its
# crossed windows become a diagnostic. Nothing here is run into collapse on purpose.
#
# SPLIT: seed 4 fits, seed 5 is held out. Precondition checked FIRST: warm_rows_held_out > 0.

